- ZNYX ZX342 10/100 Ethernet - DC21140 (I think - sticker covers  
chip) - This one selects speed manually - plug cable in to either the  
10baseT port or the 100base-TX port
- ZNYX AZ345Q 10/100 Ethernet w/ WOL - DC21143 (I think - sticker  
covers chip)
- SMC 8434T 2-port 10baseT Ethernet - 2x DC21040
- SMC 8432BT 10baseT Ethernet - DC21041
- SMC 9332DST 10/100 Ethernet - DC21140
- 2x DEC DE435 "EtherWorks Turbo" - DC21040
- Adaptec ANA-6944A/TX 4-port 10/100 Ethernet - 4x DC21140-AE
- 2x DEC EB142 + EB142-TX daughtercard -- This is an eval /  
development board for the DC21142, and is very similar to how the  
built-in Ethernet is implemented on the Digital Personal Workstation
- DEC Tulip prototype board (!) -- chip is labeled "DC1044BA Prototype"
- SMC Tulip prototype board (!) -- chip is labeled "DC1017BA Prototype"
- DEC DC21040 10baseT prototype board (!)
- 2x DEC DE500 100base-FX Ethernet - DC21143-PC
- 2x DEC DE500 10/100 Ethernet - DC21143-PB
- Kingston KNE100TX - DC21140AC


DEC Tulip clones:

- Netgear FA310TX Rev D - LiteOn 82c169 "PNIC"
- Linksys LNE100TX Version 2.0 - LiteOn 82c115 "PNIC-II"
- Matrox NIC-100/1 - LiteOn 82c168 "PNIC"
- Generic Macronix MX98713 "PMAC"
- Generic Macronix MX98715 "PMAC"
- Generic Winbond 89c840F
- 2x Davicom DM9102 + DM9801 prototype board
- Kingston KNE110TX - not sure which clone chip this is, though I  
suspect Macronix


Other Ethernet:

- Netgear FA311 - NatSemi DP83815 - sip(4)
- Generic RTL8139 - rtk(4)
- Generic RTL8029 - ne(4)
- SMC1211TX "EZCARD 10/100" - don't remember what driver this uses
- 3Com Fast EtherLink XL - ex(4)
- SMC 9432TX "EtherPower II" - epic(4)
- Intel 82557 10/100 Ethernet - fxp(4)
- Samsung SC1200A-TX - chip is Samsung KS8920 - no driver - I have  
source code for a Linux driver for this chip


SCSI HBAs:

- Initio INI-9100UW - iha(4)
- ASUS PCI-SC200 -- Symbios 53c810A - siop(4)
- Buslogic BT-958 - bha(4)
- AdvanSys ABP-940 - adw(4)
- Adaptec AHA-2944UW - ahc(4)
- Generic NCR53c825 - siop(4)


VGA:

- Generic S3 Trip 3D/2X (86c368) AGP
- Number Nine Motion331 - S3 Trio64V+ (86c765) PCI


Audio:

- Creative Labs SoundBlaster Live!



