>> interfaces
>
> I don't see it in
>
> ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/NetBSD/packages/pkgsrc/x11/gtk2/README.html

NetBSD does not do automatic builds of all packages for all 
architectures.
I guess there are some project machines, and then there are volunteers
who do bulk builds of packages for certain architectures.

If you don't see a built package for some architecture, it does not mean
it won't work. You'll just have to download pkgsrc and build it 
yourself.

> I would think that there would be automagic scripts that build these?

There are, but there are not necessarily people who use the scripts
for some particular architecture. And I think it is unreasonable to
expect that the NetBSD project would have resources to do bulk builds
for all archs it supports.



